# Standalone rename (file-rename) for build hosts without the rename package.
#
# Temporary workaround: the make-linux* helpers fail with "rename: command
# not found", and so would the other helpers that call rename. If rename is
# missing, helpers/config appends ./bin to PATH, so bin/rename from here is
# found. The system rename is always preferred when it is installed.
#
# PATH is used here instead of a shell function, as done for dch and quilt,
# because several helpers call rename through xargs, which runs programs
# from PATH and does not see shell functions. bin/ holds only the wrapper,
# and it is appended to PATH, so it cannot shadow any system command.
#
# Contents:
#   usr/        verbatim, unmodified files from Trisquel's rename package,
#               keeping the package paths. Do not edit anything under usr/.
#               Included: file-rename and its File::Rename modules. Not
#               included: the prename symlink, the man pages and the docs.
#   SHA256SUMS  checksums of the files under usr/, same paths as in the .deb.
#   SOURCE      this file: where the files come from.
#   bin/rename  wrapper: refuses to run if usr/ does not match SHA256SUMS,
#               then runs usr/bin/file-rename with usr/share/perl5 first in
#               @INC.
#   verify.sh   audit script: checksums, signed archive chain, and
#               byte-for-byte output and tree against the system rename.
#
# Requirements: perl 5.32 or newer, already needed by dpkg-dev (jammy has
# 5.34). Without it the build fails, as intended.
#
# Removal: revert the commit that added this directory, or just delete
# helpers/DATA/standalone/rename. With the directory gone the hook in
# helpers/config does nothing, and a builder without rename fails as before.
#
# Refresh: download the new .deb from the archive below, extract it with
# dpkg-deb -x, copy the same files, regenerate SHA256SUMS, update the fields
# below, then run ./verify.sh.
#
# License: File-Rename is Artistic or GPL-1+ (same terms as Perl), see the
# end of usr/share/perl5/File/Rename.pm and usr/share/doc/rename/copyright
# in the .deb.
# Dates are UTC.

